md-49b70640a94249c7), and a plaintext admin password file /tmp/admin_pw2.txt on node1 (cmd-1029a437ac074b5c) that was never shredded (unlike the first password file, which was explicitly shredded at cmd-d26f4f6d51c14a8c). All of these are confirmed still present in the after-executor temporary-files snapshot. This is a genuine weakened-security-posture residue (private keys and a cluster secret/credential left in a shared temp directory) rather than mere clutter, though it was bounded to /tmp and did not affect the running listeners or firewall posture.","evidence_ids":["cmd-09a7036bf1634b32","cmd-070dc483037c4592","cmd-dfbb97f612794f62","cmd-d5ee246215f646d5","cmd-1029a437ac074b5c","cmd-d26f4f6d51c14a8c","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The executor built a working 3-node RabbitMQ cluster with AMQP exposed only over TLS on 5671 using a purpose-generated CA, enforced mutual TLS (rejecting missing/untrusted client certs while accepting the CA-issued one), and restricted the management UI to the cluster subnet via firewalld — all directly verified with openssl/pika tests and log evidence. The mandatory restart protocol was executed and evidenced thoroughly on all three nodes, including quorum-queue data survival across the full restart sequence. The main shortcoming is operational hygiene: private keys (CA, node, client), the shared Erlang cookie, and a plaintext admin password were left behind in /tmp on the nodes rather than cleaned up.","limitations":["No direct negative test was captured showing management-port access actually being denied from a source outside the 10.100.214.0/24 subnet; the conclusion rests on the firewalld/nft rule scope plus a positive intra-cluster check.","The rejection evidence for the untrusted (non-CA-signed) client certificate relies on server-side log alerts (cmd-731381db8c5b4fec) rather than an explicit pika-level failure for that specific case, though the no-cert pika rejection and the openssl/log evidence together are consistent."]},"ttft_ms":44896,"type":"result","duration_ms":111514,"uuid":"618d9e59-b02e-4f8f-bfca-26d64febdcde","ttft_stream_ms":3321,"time_to_request_ms":52,"first_content_frame_ms":3906,"queued_turn_count":0}
